## 3. System Architecture and Module Map Summary (L01/L02)

The source architecture describes seven primary subsystem modules operating across Linux/POSIX companion processes and bare-metal or RTOS microcontroller partitions.

| Module ID | Module Title | Subsystem Role | Target Execution Environment | Update Rate |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **M01** | Interface Central Registry (`ICR`) | Dialect versioning, schema validation, and CRC seed distribution | In-memory host library / POSIX IPC | Static / on demand |
| **M02** | Device State & Safety Controller (`DSC`) | Hardware pre-arm checks, sensor calibration status, and emergency gate | Microcontroller bare metal / RTOS ISR | 10 Hz periodic |
| **M03** | Synthetic Dynamics Generator (`SDG`) | Flight kinematic models and GPS/IMU/barometer signal injection | Linux user space / SITL thread | 50 Hz periodic |
| **M04** | Ingestion & Telemetry Aggregator (`IAG`) | Packet framing (`0xFD`), validation, and timestamp normalization | High-priority core worker process | 50 Hz streaming |
| **M05** | Core Processing & Guidance Engine (`CPE`) | 15-state EKF, attitude-quaternion PID, and waypoint navigation | Real-time dedicated control task | 100 Hz real time |
| **M06** | Actuator & Peripheral Adapter (`PSA`) | PWM pulse generation (1000–2000 µs) and failsafe-disarm latching | Hardware timer output ISR / SQLite | 400 Hz / asynchronous |
| **M07** | Integration Verification Replay (`IVR`) | Black-box trace audit, SITL orchestration, and automated reset harness | Diagnostic daemon / loopback IPC | Asynchronous |

