## 4. Master Interface Contract Specifications (L03)

The source material describes seven binary interface contracts connecting the modules.

### 4.1 Interface Flow Overview

```text
              [M01: Interface Central Registry (ICR)]
                              |
                 IF-01: Schema Query & CRC Seeds
                       /                \
                      v                  v
       [M03: Synthetic Dynamics]   [M02: Device State Controller]
                      |                  |
             IF-03: 50 Hz          IF-02: 10 Hz
             Kinematics            Pre-Arm Gate
                      \                  /
                       v                v
                 [M04: Ingestion & Aggregator]
                              |
               IF-04: Normalized Canonical Frame
                              |
                              v
                 [M05: Core Processing Engine]
                              |
                 IF-05: Actuator Control PWM
                              |
                              v
                 [M06: Actuator Output Adapter]
                              |
                 IF-06: Diagnostic Flight Trace
                              |
                              v
              [M07: Verification & Replay Harness]
                              ^
                              |
                    IF-07: SITL Reset & Sync
                              |
                         [M02 / M03]
```

### 4.2 Detailed Interface Descriptions

- **`IF-01` – Telemetry and Schema Distribution:** Provides Semantic Versioning (SemVer) schema verification (`0x010200`) and message CRC32 hashes. The stated goal is to avoid schema mismatches between the companion computer and flight controller.
- **`IF-02` – Flight Readiness and Pre-Arm Gate:** A periodic 10 Hz heartbeat carrying a 32-bit atomic bitmask representing IMU health, GPS 3D fix, RC link state, battery-voltage threshold, and arming permissives.
- **`IF-03` – Synthetic Flight and Sensor Stream:** A 50 Hz kinematic telemetry stream framed with the `0xFD` marker, sequential packet IDs, sensor payload, and 16-bit X.25 CRC.
- **`IF-04` – Validated Canonical Flight Frame:** A normalized flight-state frame delivered to the EKF using SI units: acceleration in `m/s²`, angular rate in `rad/s`, and pressure in `Pa`.
- **`IF-05` – GNC State, Actuator, and ACK Stream:** Motor-mixer commands translate normalized roll, pitch, yaw, and thrust values into ESC pulse-width modulation signals from `1000 µs` to `2000 µs`.
- **`IF-06` – Telemetry Audit and Flight Trace:** A non-blocking circular trace logger records flight anomalies, state changes, and packet drops to persistent storage.
- **`IF-07` – SITL Orchestration and Reset Command:** A synchronization interface through which automated tests can request origin snaps, kinematic-vector resets, and hardware-state clears.

